## Goal
Perform a principal component analysis (PCA) of the gene count matrix to visualize transcriptional clustering of samples. The plot will be colored by experimental condition (treated vs. untreated) to reveal whether samples cluster primarily by treatment effect.

## Inputs
Artifact types resolve through each sub-stage's OUTPUTS.tsv at execution time; the paths
below are what they resolve to today.

| Artifact type | Resolved from | Path |
|---|---|---|
| counts_gene | 02_bioinformatics/rnaseq_bulk/01_nfcore-rnaseq-wrapper | 02_bioinformatics/rnaseq_bulk/01_nfcore-rnaseq-wrapper/run/results/star_salmon/salmon.merged.gene_counts_length_scaled.tsv |

## Method
1. Load gene count matrix from the resolved counts_gene artifact using R and the DESeq2 package in conda environment gars-bio.
2. Filter genes with low expression (keep genes with count-per-million ≥ 1 in at least 2 samples) to remove noise.
3. Apply variance-stabilizing transformation (DESeq2::vst) to normalize and stabilize variance across the count range.
4. Perform PCA on the transformed counts matrix using the prcomp function.
5. Extract sample metadata (sample_id and condition) from the project's samples.csv file in 00_data/rnaseq_bulk/.
6. Create a scatter plot of PC1 vs. PC2, with points colored by condition (untreated=blue, treated=red); include sample labels and percentage of variance explained for each axis.
7. Generate a scree plot showing cumulative variance explained by the first 10 principal components.
8. Save PCA scores (sample coordinates for all PCs) and variance explained table to CSV format.

